CloudBurrow patch 8 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1111).

The bug: a RANGE value in a query's result (SELECT RANGE(DATE '2020-01-01',
DATE '2020-02-01')) was answered with a schema field of no type, at the top
level, in an ARRAY or in a STRUCT (measured through CloudBurrow's front), as
TableFieldSchemaFromColumnType had no case for GoogleSQL's TYPE_RANGE (30),
so no client could read it: the Go client fails "incomplete range schema".
Its value was GoogleSQL's text, a TIMESTAMP bound as
"2020-01-01 00:00:00.000000+00" and a DATETIME bound with a space, where
BigQuery's REST API gives int64 microseconds and a "T" (the forms the
official Go client parses, cloud.google.com/go/bigquery convertRangeValue,
and its value_test.go).

The patch gives a RANGE column the type RANGE and rangeElementType (also
for an ARRAY of them), and Format writes a top-level RANGE value, or a
REPEATED one's, in the REST form. A RANGE inside a STRUCT gets its schema
but not the value rewrite (Format does not walk STRUCTs).

